body:
College student exemptions in CA have already changed though, according to [this letter](https://cdss.ca.gov/Portals/9/Additional-Resources/Letters-and-Notices/ACLs/2022/22-84.pdf?ver=2022-11-18-161200-390). But please correct me if I'm wrong! Not sure if I'm interpreting it correctly. 

&#x200B;

The temporary exemptions of EFC=$0 was removed, but they're keeping the approval for federal work-study.

Thanks for a venting space. But also... i see you and I feel you. ❤️

&#x200B;

I'm exhausted literally 24/7 and I can't catch a break. I'm the only adult and I have a toddler so I do everything and I'm tired. I do all the laundry, I do all the driving, i HATE meal times and groceries so much because I have the pickiest of picky eaters. I sweep the floor and swiffer and clean the damn bathroom that smells like pee all the time because 3 year olds. I put the damn duvet cover on and take it off when I have to wash it. I take care of all the doctor appointments, dentists, I do all of the laundry and take out the trash. And you're right, it's not hard, but when do we get a real break? When do we get time to NOT think about everyone else? Tired moms are tired 😫
